  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reflexive in the dative",
     "texto": [
      "In **Ich wasche mich**, the reflexive pronoun is accusative. If the action includes a body part as the direct object, the reflexive goes in the dative: **Ich wasche mir die Hände**.",
      "It is not a rule for any complement: the verb and its other objects determine the case. With body parts an article is normally used: **die Hände**, not «meine Hände»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Purchases and own things",
     "texto": [
      "**Ich kaufe mir ein Auto** (I buy myself a car). **Ich putze mir die Zähne** (I brush my teeth). **Du bürstest dir die Haare** (you brush your hair).",
      "Once you know the object, the reflexive changes: mich → mir."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Person",
     "columnas": [
